Define the tax rates as standard decimal fractions (e.g. 0.20 instead of 20) and implement rate_for to return the correct category's rate.
Replace the contents of src/checkout/tax.py with:
from decimal import Decimal

_RATES = {
    "standard": Decimal("0.20"),
    "reduced": Decimal("0.055"),
    "zero": Decimal("0"),
}


def rate_for(category: str) -> Decimal:
    return _RATES.get(category, _RATES["standard"])

